# Rootwise Survivor, Survival: "At the beginning of your second main phase, if this creature is tapped, put three +1/+1 counters on
# up to one target land you control. That land becomes a 0/0 Elemental creature in addition to its other types. It gains haste until
# your next turn." Rootwise (haste) is cast on turn 3 and attacks, so it is tapped at the second main phase. Bot2's Island is no
# target (the refusal: "you control", CR 115.1), Bot1's Forest is. The Forest gets three counters and becomes a 0/0 Elemental
# creature that is still a Forest land (3/3 with the counters, CR 613.1d, 613.4c); the Island beside it is untouched. The haste lasts
# through Bot2's turn 4 (until Bot1's next turn begins, CR 611.2a) and is gone on turn 5, while the creature and its counters stay.

